The Planetary Shape Model and Ray Tracing System (PSMRTS) was orginally
developed by the the OSIRIS-APEX team. The work is derived from mission support
activities that transpired during OSIRIS-REx proximity operations in support of
global and regional high-precision cartograhic operations prior to, during and
after sample acquisiton from the surface of asteroid 101955 Bennu. Some of the
concepts herein were orginally developed in a version of the Integrated Software
for Imagers and Spectometers (ISIS) derived from a public release of ISIS and
maintained by the OSIRIS-REx mission team at the University of Arizona.

PSMRTS was funded by the OSIRIS-APEX project with intent to be reincorporated
back into ISIS for public release in preparation for proximity operations of
asteroid 99942 Apophis.

- Kris J. Becker (University of Arizona)
- Kyle A. Becker (University of Arizona)
- Kenneth L. Edmundson (University of Arizona)
